{"5101960":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Dungeons & Dynasties","steam_appid":5101960,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Football Manager, but every match is a dungeon and your players can die in it.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You run an adventuring guild in a realm that lost its king. Sign delvers, swear them to a term of years and send them into the dark. Win enough and you take the Crucible, and hold the realm until somebody takes it off you.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Heroes die. Dynasties rise. The realm remembers both.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/extras\/d0718a710529c9864f7e4370f14976b7.avif?t=1793728816\" width=966 height=532 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Every fixture is a dungeon<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is no match engine. Each delve is built for the day, and in the Trials a rival guild goes into the same one. If they make it to the final room, you fight them there.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You never click an attack. You pick the party, set their orders and kit them out, then you watch. Flooded ground slows your fighters and pitch dark ruins your archers, so who you send matters as much as how strong they are. Nine classes, ten races, and a party that grows from four to six as you climb six divisions.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >People, not numbers<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every delver arrives believing something, struggling with something, and swearing to do one thing before they are done. Most never manage it. Sending the right one on the right work, year after year, is how you find out who they are.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >They make friends and grudges underground. They sign for a term of years and come back asking for what they are worth. They pick up scars, retire, get sold, or do not come home, and the dead get a memorial card with their own sigil and epitaph. The Dungeonborn are the ones that you bring back.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/extras\/5d946821cf78183bda0d9a05c4656ca5.avif?t=1793728816\" width=1202 height=638 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A realm that goes on without you<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seventy-two guilds hold seats in 36 towns across seven lands, so you share a street with somebody who wanted to better you before a fixture was ever played. Rival halls sign, sell, rise and fall. Wars are called and the realm remembers who marched. Beasts roam the roads, and below everything the Deep goes down further than anyone has been.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your own hall stands in a real town that you can build up, defend, and one day watch your retired delvers settle in.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Chronicle<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your guild has been writing it down the whole time. Open the Chronicle and the dynasty is there as a story, season by season, with the fallen and the legends who made the place what it is. Everything in it happened in your save.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Play it your way<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Climb from the Backwater or start higher up. Take a patron's backing or go it alone. Stack any of the founding terms you like, from Ironman to a guild made entirely of beasts, or play Cozy Mode with no league at all and simply run the guild.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > 72 rival guilds, six divisions, a cup and the Crucible<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > A full transfer market, with free transfers, loans, poaching and fire sales<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Training, a youth academy and mentors<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Your hometown to build up and defend<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Vows, families, scars and permanent death<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Over a dozen founding terms that all stack, and Cozy Mode<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Twelve languages besides English<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The dungeon is waiting, Guildmaster.<\/p>","about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Football Manager, but every match is a dungeon and your players can die in it.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You run an adventuring guild in a realm that lost its king. Sign delvers, swear them to a term of years and send them into the dark. Win enough and you take the Crucible, and hold the realm until somebody takes it off you.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Heroes die. Dynasties rise. The realm remembers both.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/extras\/d0718a710529c9864f7e4370f14976b7.avif?t=1793728816\" width=966 height=532 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Every fixture is a dungeon<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is no match engine. Each delve is built for the day, and in the Trials a rival guild goes into the same one. If they make it to the final room, you fight them there.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You never click an attack. You pick the party, set their orders and kit them out, then you watch. Flooded ground slows your fighters and pitch dark ruins your archers, so who you send matters as much as how strong they are. Nine classes, ten races, and a party that grows from four to six as you climb six divisions.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >People, not numbers<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every delver arrives believing something, struggling with something, and swearing to do one thing before they are done. Most never manage it. Sending the right one on the right work, year after year, is how you find out who they are.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >They make friends and grudges underground. They sign for a term of years and come back asking for what they are worth. They pick up scars, retire, get sold, or do not come home, and the dead get a memorial card with their own sigil and epitaph. The Dungeonborn are the ones that you bring back.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/extras\/5d946821cf78183bda0d9a05c4656ca5.avif?t=1793728816\" width=1202 height=638 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A realm that goes on without you<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seventy-two guilds hold seats in 36 towns across seven lands, so you share a street with somebody who wanted to better you before a fixture was ever played. Rival halls sign, sell, rise and fall. Wars are called and the realm remembers who marched. Beasts roam the roads, and below everything the Deep goes down further than anyone has been.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your own hall stands in a real town that you can build up, defend, and one day watch your retired delvers settle in.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Chronicle<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your guild has been writing it down the whole time. Open the Chronicle and the dynasty is there as a story, season by season, with the fallen and the legends who made the place what it is. Everything in it happened in your save.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Play it your way<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Climb from the Backwater or start higher up. Take a patron's backing or go it alone. Stack any of the founding terms you like, from Ironman to a guild made entirely of beasts, or play Cozy Mode with no league at all and simply run the guild.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > 72 rival guilds, six divisions, a cup and the Crucible<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > A full transfer market, with free transfers, loans, poaching and fire sales<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Training, a youth academy and mentors<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Your hometown to build up and defend<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Vows, families, scars and permanent death<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Over a dozen founding terms that all stack, and Cozy Mode<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Twelve languages besides English<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The dungeon is waiting, Guildmaster.<\/p>","short_description":"DnD meets Football Manager. Create a guild, watch them form relationships and grow old together. Lose people both to the dark and to rival guilds battling to be the best in the realm. Grow your own town, or vote to help build an existing one. Or take the Cozy approach and run a guild on your terms.","supported_languages":"English, French, German, Spanish - Spain, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Spanish - Latin America, Korean, Italian, Russian, Portuguese - Brazil, Portuguese - Portugal","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/b410c700f03fb3f65478e393cf864f90e7a1a57c\/header.jpg?t=1793728816","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/59efdb6296ab7a63966a4ef5ca0885c1ed59ef1a\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793728816","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5101960\/59efdb6296ab7a63966a4ef5ca0885c1ed59ef1a\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793728816","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 (64-bit)<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Any 64-bit dual-core processor<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 MB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Integrated Graphics<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 150 MB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Sound Card:<\/strong> Any<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Requires the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, which is included with Windows 10 (1803 and later) and Windows 11. The installer will add it if it is missing.<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 11 (64-bit)<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Windows 11 (64-bit)<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 MB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Integrated Graphics<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 250 MB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Sound Card:<\/strong> Any<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> A larger display shows more of the ledger at once. Designed for 1280x720 and above.<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":[],"linux_requirements":[],"developers":["Bretticus82"],"publishers":["Surefire.Games"],"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","initial":899,"final":809,"discount_percent":10,"initial_formatted":"$8.99","final_formatted":"$8.09"},"packages":[1767439],"package_groups":[{"name":"default","title":"Buy Dungeons & Dynasties","description":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","save_text":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","subs":[{"packageid":1767439,"percent_savings_text":"-10% ","percent_savings":0,"opti